      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Goldthwaite once earned the nickname 'City of Windmills' because almost every household had a water well by 1900.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldthwaite%2C_Texas",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1905 Confederate Reunion in Goldthwaite drew the largest crowd in Mills County history, marking a significant social event.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/goldthwaite-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The county’s first school library opened in 1915, the same year construction began on Lake Merritt, just seven miles from town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
